{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Over him.</b> Over the people." "<b>Taskmasters.</b> From the root מַס — officers who collect the tax from them. And what is the מַס? That they build store-cities for Pharaoh." "<b>In their burdens.</b> Of Egypt." "<b>Store-cities.</b> As the Targum renders it; and so ״לֶךְ בֹּא אֶל הַסֹּכֵן הַזֶּה״ (Isaiah 22) — a treasurer appointed over the treasuries." "<b>Pithom and Raamses.</b> That they were not fit for this at first, and they made them strong and fortified for a treasury."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:05.031202066Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}